  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "So, you've got a list of small jobs around the house and you're thinking of calling a handyman. That's a smart move for those tasks that don't quite warrant a specialist but are beyond your DIY comfort zone. When you're looking for a handyman, you'll want to clearly describe the problems you're facing. Pictures are a huge help here! Once they understand the scope, they should provide you with a written quote. Don't be shy about asking if they bill hourly or by the job—it's crucial for budgeting. Make sure you understand what's included and, just as importantly, what isn't. For example, will they haul away debris? HH Remodeling LLC is all about clear communication, so we'll walk you through every step. Always confirm who exactly will be doing the work and if there's any warranty or guarantee on the service. This clarity helps avoid surprises down the road and ensures your satisfaction. Ready to get those tasks checked off your list? Let's talk about your home repair needs."
    }
  ],
